Subject: ENTS Playwright automation - October update

Hi Gurpreet,

Here's a quick summary of what we got done on the Playwright migration in October, with the ENTS parts first.

ENTS
- The ENTS test cases (TC_01_ENTS to TC_25_ENTS) are running on the new Playwright framework, with test data pulled from Oracle into the Test Data Vault at the start of each run (TC_00_DATA).
- TC_01_ENTS now copes with a transferor that has no entitlements to select: it marks that herd as not usable and picks a new transferor/transferee pair automatically (up to 3 times). Fixed-data runs stop with a clear message instead. TC_08_ENTS also reports this case clearly.
- ENTS now has its own daily Jenkins run, Monday to Friday at about 07:00. The first scheduled run on 19 October completed all 26 test cases in about 70 minutes. It found some failures, which I'm working through now.

Jenkins / CI (shared with BISS)
- The framework now runs on the DAFM OpenShift Jenkins, with the DB and test data files held in an OpenShift secret set up by the platform team, so nothing sensitive sits in GitLab.
- First fully green pipeline run on 16 October, after fixing a Chromium start-up issue in the OpenShift pod.
- Build with Parameters now has a SUITE option (BISS, ENTS or a custom list of test cases), and BISS also runs daily at about 05:00.
- Each build shows its pass/fail counts in the build history, and has a "Test Dashboard" link with the team report and a masked stakeholder report (the PDF version is under Build Artifacts). The dashboard currently looks plain because of Jenkins' security settings. I've asked the platform team about the setting that fixes it.

BISS (for context)
- Migrated the staff test cases in four batches, plus fixes for partnership herds in TC_03_PART (the partnership popup, partner herd tabs and paging in Land Details).
- Reworked TC_12 so the same journeys aren't repeated, and added handling for the Protein Aid Scheme "no eligible crop" popup.

Next steps
- Triage and fix the ENTS daily-run failures.
- Get the Jenkins report styling sorted with the platform team.
- Carry on migrating the remaining staff test cases.

Happy to go through any of this, or show you the Jenkins jobs, if that's useful.

Thanks,
